  "worked_solution": "First, we rearrange our equation into a form that is more convenient for logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{7}^{5x}+8 & =34 \\\\ {7}^{5x} & =26\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take ${log}_{7}$ of both sides of the equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{7}^{5x} & =26 \\\\ {log}_{7}⁡({7}^{5x}) & ={log}_{7}⁡(26) \\\\ 5x & ={log}_{7}⁡(26) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{5}{log}_{7}⁡(26)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above on a calculator gives\n\n$$\nx≈0.335\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.",
